course: dictionary
lesson: 5165
title: Irritating: annoying or sore
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Irritating has two meanings, and the context tells you which one is used. Something irritating is annoying, like a dripping tap or a buzzing fly, because it makes you feel cross or impatient. Ask yourself: what does the sentence say the thing does?
explain: «Nettle hairs are tiny glass-like needles that break off and inject an irritating mix into the skin.» Here irritating is about the body. The clue is in the same sentence: «the sting hurts and itches». Try the annoying meaning in the sentence and it does not fit, but "a mix that makes skin sore" does.
explain: Irritating comes from the verb irritate, which means to annoy or to make a part of the body sore. So you can use the word to describe a thing, as in «an irritating habit», or a feeling on the skin, as in «irritating to the skin».
fact: Irritating means annoying, making you feel cross or impatient.
fact: Irritating can also mean making a part of the body sore, itchy or red.
fact: Irritating comes from the verb irritate, so it can be used as a verb form too.
fact: Phrases to notice: «really irritating», «an irritating habit», «irritating to the skin».
fact: In science and safety, a chemical labelled «irritant» can be irritating to skin and eyes.
exercise: Sam says, «The buzzing fly was really irritating.» What does irritating mean here? | *Annoying, making you feel cross | Making skin red and sore | Quiet and gentle | Very cold
exercise: «The nettle's mix is irritating to the skin.» What does irritating mean here? | Keeping the skin warm | *Making the skin sore and itchy | Annoying a friend | Making people laugh
exercise: Which words in «the sting hurts and itches» are the clue that irritating is about the body? | *hurts and itches | grazing animals | glass-like | leaves
test: Mia says her little brother's humming is irritating. Which meaning is she using? | Quiet as a whisper | *Annoying, making her cross | Glowing with light | Sore and itchy on the skin
test: Which meaning fits «an irritating habit»? | Sad and tired | *Annoying, something that makes people cross | Making the skin red and sore | Giving out light
exam: Which sentence uses irritating to mean making the body sore? | The irritating song played all day. | The irritating tap dripped all night. | *Smoke from the bonfire was irritating to her eyes. | My irritating sister keeps humming.
